{"availability":"available","full":"0x5066/WinampVisWASM","name":"WinampVisWASM","description":"(Some) Winamp internals ported to Webassembly making use of the Web Audio API for delivering the audio","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":6,"forks":2,"created":"2024-12-17T11:42:42Z","updated":"2025-01-09T21:23:35Z","license":"WTFPL","branch":"main","homepage":"https://0x5066.github.io/WinampVisWASM/draw_sa.html","topics":[],"demo":"https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=ms-vscode.live-server","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T00:26:13.567Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T00:26:13.567Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T00:26:13.567Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T00:26:13.567Z","stars":6,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This is a project to study and understand how Winamp gets the audio for visualization.","Through this, the web browser acts as both the \"Input plugin\" and \"Winamp\" at the same time, as the \"Input plugin\" portion of this project (although in a very crude form, as the call to saaddpcmdata is called in a thread to simulate Winamp calling the play() function in a plugin) provides \"Winamp\" (also the browser) with the audio data needed to process and visualize, thanks to the Web Audio API.","The \"Winamp\" portion is the simple audio player controls, visualizer and upload button, aka the frontend."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/0x5066/WinampVisWASM/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1dd71d0d4c5c438c401f600ee6e714f1d9937aaed283491825aecfef9e3fe5bf","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T00:26:13.655Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T00:26:13.655Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This is a project to study and understand how Winamp gets the audio for visualization.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/0x5066/WinampVisWASM/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"1dd71d0d4c5c438c401f600ee6e714f1d